bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    rv32imac_decode_spec_needs_m_extension_and_jump_branch_decode_2026-11-27, 0, "test/01_unit/hardware/rv32imac/rv32_decode_spec.spl imported hardware.rv32imac.core.rv32_decode / pkg.rv32_isa_pkg / pkg.rv32_types_pkg, which never existed in git history (the old tree was src/hardware/rv32gc, deleted in 4cf561567fe, with a different rv32_decode_inst API). The field/immediate decoders now live in hardware.riscv_common (restored by 5b7c26c65a1), so the spec was retargeted there; its 8 field/immediate/ALU cases pass in rv32_decode_spec.spl. The other 6, split into test/01_unit/hardware/rv32imac/rv32_decode_m_ext_jump_spec.spl (in-development), need an RV32IMAC decoder that does not exist: AluOp has no Mul (M extension: decode_alu_op(OP_OP, 0, 0x01) -> Mul), and decode_branch_op takes only funct3, while the spec calls decode_branch_op(opcode, funct3) and expects Jal/Jalr for OP_JAL/OP_JALR and None for a non-branch opcode. Fix: add the M-extension ALU ops and an opcode-aware branch/jump decode to riscv_common (or an rv32imac layer over it), then drop the in-development tag (and fold the cases back if wanted)."

